# Keep the build context small AND correct.
#
# node_modules MUST be excluded: the Dockerfile runs `npm ci` (installing
# Linux-native builds of sharp/bcrypt/prisma) and then `COPY . .`. Without this
# file that COPY would paste the host's node_modules - built for the developer's
# OS - straight over the container's, and the native modules would fail to load
# at runtime. It also stops hundreds of MB being uploaded to the build host.
node_modules
dist
build
coverage

# Never ship secrets or local env into an image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.gitignore
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Tests / tooling not needed at runtime
test
**/*.spec.ts
.eslintrc*
eslint.config.*
.prettierrc*

# NOTE: storage/media is deliberately NOT ignored - the Dockerfile bakes it into
# the image so the Render free-tier demo keeps its images/PDFs across restarts
# (see backend/.gitignore and DEPLOYMENT.md).
